<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trajan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">53–117 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trajan was Roman emperor from 98 to 117 CE, under whom the empire reached its greatest territorial extent. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a> in two wars and later campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a>, annexing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> for a time. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> discuss him in the context of its military history, and his reign is traditionally regarded as one of the high points of the Roman principate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trajan.jpg" alt="Trajan" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Traianus_Glyptothek_Munich_72.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
